{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n**R01: Legal Order & Authority**\nNo evidence for legal order, recommendation, execution, check, or closure authority is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind legal authority; no source-grounded basis for order issuance.\n\n**R02: Hazard Triggers & Zone Sequencing**\n[S15] mandates binding decisions to a specific forecast cycle, with expiry at the next update or material field observation [S15]. The conservative operational envelope applies until field observations rule out adverse branches; a better median alone does not cancel protective actions [S15]. Aircraft infrared mapping can lag by two hours under smoke, so absence of a new perimeter is not proof fire spread stopped [S15]. [S04] notes South Pass closes under smoke visibility below 150 meters and North Bridge excludes full-size buses above 54°C [S04].\n*   **Disposition:** Partial. Trigger logic exists in [S15], but zone sequencing specific to fire behavior is absent.\n*   **Qualifications:** Forecast revisions must not be mixed; adverse-branch actions are required [S15]. Smoke and heat conditions invalidate routes post-plan [S04].\n*   **Blockers:** Missing explicit fire triggers independent of weather ensemble; no expiry logic defined for physical route constraints.\n\n**R03: Population Basis & Assistance Demand**\n[S03] specifies Zone A (5,280), B (8,940), C (12,600) residents plus up to 2,100 tourists [S03]. Survey coverage is 91% [S03]. Categories (no vehicle, mobility, oxygen, dialysis) overlap and must not be summed as independent people [S03].\n*   **Disposition:** Accepted with qualification.\n*   **Qualifications:** Must carry uncertainty allowance for unreported households; cannot treat unregistered as self-evacuating [S03]. Tourist demand is time-dependent [S03].\n*   **Blockers:** None identified in source, but overlap logic must be enforced to avoid double-counting.\n\n**R04: Road Bottlenecks & Route Clearance**\n[S04] establishes Mill Junction as the system bottleneck with a measured sustainable throughput of 1,500 vehicles/hour [S04]. North Bridge (1,100 veh/h) and South Pass (850 veh/h) feed into Mill Junction; their capacities cannot be added [S04]. Last exercise achieved only 1,180 veh/h at Mill Junction due to unmanaged lane merging [S04], a defect confirmed open in multiple records within [S13] [S13].\n*   **Disposition:** Accepted.\n*   **Qualifications:** Do not sum independent road ratings across the shared downstream bottleneck [S04]. Clearance time must use shared junction and exercise throughput until a current field test proves otherwise [S04], [S13].\n*   **Blockers:** Contraflow requires sheriff closure, 45 minutes setup, and staffed crossover points [S04]. County 12 cannot be fully converted to outbound traffic [S04].\n\n**R05: Fleet Matching & Driver Duty**\n[S13] records lift-bus dispatch delays of up to 129 minutes in exercise records EX-007 and EX-019, with status open or repaired inconsistently across cycles [S13]. No evidence for person/accommodation-level fleet matching, driver duty cycles, bridge constraints specific to vehicle types (beyond S04 bus exclusion), or relief capacity is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind fleet requirements; no cycle time data available beyond defect logs.\n\n**R06: Shelter Capacity & Medical Handoffs**\n[S13] indicates Civic Arena opened, while Ridge School’s filter test failed in the exercise [S13]. Shelter-filter defects remain open in records EX-004, EX-028, EX-034, EX-040, and EX-046 [S13]. No evidence for smoke-safe shelter capacity, accessible placements, medical handoffs, filtration, power, or relocation is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot verify shelter suitability or medical continuity; filter failures unresolved.\n\n**R07: Warnings & Community Support**\n[S13] notes County radio voice worked, but volunteer unit identifiers did not cross the gateway in the exercise [S13]. Radio-handoff defects persist in open records EX-014, EX-020, EX-026, EX-032, and EX-044 [S13]. No evidence for redundant multilingual warning, door-knock timing, radio interoperability standards, receipt/understanding evidence, or zone revision is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind communication strategy; gateway interoperability failure unresolved.\n\n**R08: Fuel & Power Continuity**\n[S13] records fuel arrival after seventeen hours in the exercise, with open defects EX-005, EX-011, EX-035, EX-041, and EX-047 [S13]. No evidence for fuel/power continuity, observed delays beyond 17-hour benchmark, local staging, alternate routes/suppliers, or coupled asset effects is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind resource contracting; fuel delay exceeds operational targets.\n\n**R09: Animals & Service Animals**\nNo evidence for animal handling or service animal separation without delaying human evacuation is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind animal logistics.\n\n**R10: Accountability & Data Privacy**\n[S13] records family-accountability defects, with open items EX-021, EX-027, EX-033, and EX-039 [S13]. No evidence for private accountability, public aggregation, self-evacuation tracking, restricted health data handling, reconciliation, retention, or deletion proof is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind data management protocol; accountability defects open.\n\n**R11: 48-Hour Execution Sequence**\nNo evidence for a concrete 48-hour sequence with owners, effects, current checks, repair, recheck, resource/cost authority, and contingencies is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind execution timeline.\n\n**R12: Verification & Readiness Blockers**\n[S13] states readiness requires current execution evidence for the exact plan rather than a status label, and owner attestation is not operational proof [S13]. Exercise values override nominal targets until repair is rechecked [S13]. No evidence for independent-review blockers, candidate-bound readiness, uncertainties, or explicit falsifiers is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Partial. Verification logic exists in [S13], but specific blockers are undefined.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot verify readiness status; open defects in [S13] block closure.\n\n**Cross-Source Relationships & Contradictions**\n[S03] defines demand (population, assistance categories) while [S04] defines supply constraints (road throughput, junction bottlenecks). [S15] provides temporal binding (forecast cycles) that dictates when [S04] route viability and [S03] population risk assessments are valid. [S13] provides the verification layer, overriding nominal capacities in [S04] with observed exercise defects. No contradictions exist between sources, but [S13] explicitly invalidates reliance on nominal targets from [S04] until rechecks pass.\n\n**Unresolved Evidence**\n*   Specific trigger values for fire/weather (R02) are absent"}}],"created":1787627433,"model":"Qwen3.8-27B-AD-IQ2_S.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10434-7e4c0a968","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":1900,"prompt_tokens":6258,"total_tokens":8158,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-pFcRhqP2p4g6ko1mpH6hadznZ4mDzLeA","__verbose":{"index":0,"content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n**R01: Legal Order & Authority**\nNo evidence for legal order, recommendation, execution, check, or closure authority is present in [S03], [S04], [S13], or [S15].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.